<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Colonial Sugar Refining Company</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1855</span> · Also known as CSR Limited</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Colonial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">Sugar</a> Refining Company was an Australian sugar company founded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-nova-scotia">Sydney</a> in 1855. It expanded into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fiji">Fiji</a> in the 1880s, where it came to dominate the sugar industry, owning mills and estates worked largely by indentured labourers from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and later leasing land to Indo-Fijian tenant farmers. It withdrew from Fiji in 1973, when its operations passed to the Fiji government, and survives as CSR Limited.</p></div>
